@startuml
title Building and checking the random walk simulation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
  ArrowColor #2E8B67
}
start
:Define Location, Drunk, Field;
:walk(f, d, numSteps): one walk;
:simWalks(numSteps, numTrials, dClass): many walks;
:drunkTest(walkLengths, numTrials, dClass): report mean, max, min;
:Run on 10, 100, 1000, 10000 steps;
:Mean about 8.6 to 9.2 for every length;<<#FDEEEE>>
:Sanity check on 0, 1, 2 steps;
if (mean = 0 for 0 steps and 1 for 1 step?) then (no)
  :Read the code: walk() received numTrials instead of numSteps;<<#FDEEEE>>
  :Fix and re-run the sanity check;
else (yes)
endif
:Results grow with n;
:Elaborate one change at a time;
fork
  :New drunk: MasochistDrunk;
fork again
  :New field: OddField with wormholes;
end fork
:Plot distance trends, end locations, one traced walk;
:Compare with analysis: sqrt(n) and 0.05 n;
stop
@enduml
